{"r":"bhj","lane":{"p":264,"e":[{"h":"بَهُجَ","t":["aor. , (AZ, S, Msb, &c.,) inf. n. ",[2,"بَهَاجَةٌ"]," (AZ, S, L, K) and ",[2,"بَهْجَةٌ"]," (AZ, L, [but some seem to regard this as a simple subst.,]) and ",[2,"بَهَجَانٌ"],", (L,) ",[1,"He,"]," or ",[1,"it, was,"]," or ",[1,"became, beautiful,"]," or ",[1,"goodly:"]," (AZ, S, L, Msb, K:) or ",[1,"beautiful in colour:"]," or ",[1,"beautiful and bright"]," or ",[1,"splendid:"]," or ",[1,"it"]," (a plant) ",[1,"was,"]," or ",[1,"became, beautiful and bright;"]," and ",[1,"he"]," (a man) ",[1,"was,"]," or ",[1,"became, characterized by a laughing,"]," or ",[1,"happy, appearance of the beautiful parts of the face, as the cheeks, and the lines of the forehead:"]," or ",[1,"by the appearance of joy, gladness,"]," or ",[1,"happiness;"]," or ",[1,"by a joyful, glad,"]," or ",[1,"happy, aspect,"]," or ",[1,"appearance."]," (L.) You say also, ",[2,"بَهِجَ"],[2,"النَّبَاتُ"],", with kesr, meaning (assumed tropical:) ",[1,"The plant,"]," or ",[1,"herbage, was,"]," or ",[1,"became, beautiful"]," [&c.]. (TA, [but this is probably a tropical signification, from ",[2,"بَهِجَ"]," in the sense here following.]) ― -b2- ",[2,"بَهِجَ"],", (S, A, L, K,) with kesr, (S,) aor. , (K,) inf. n. ",[2,"بَهَجٌ"],"; (L;) and ↓ ",[2,"ابتهج"],"; (S, A, L, Msb, K;) ",[1,"He was,"]," or ",[1,"became, joyful, glad,"]," or ",[1,"happy."]," (S, A, L, Msb, K.) You say, ",[2,"بَهِجَ بِهِ"],", (S, A,) and ",[2,"لَهُ"],"; (TA;) and ↓ ",[2,"ابتهج"],[2,"بِهِ"],"; (A, Msb;) ",[1,"He rejoiced in it,"]," or ",[1,"at it;"]," or ",[1,"became rejoiced by it,"]," or ",[1,"at it."]," (S, A, Msb, TA.) [See also 10.] -A2- ",[2,"بَهَجَ"],", (S, K,) aor. ; (K;) and ↓ ",[2,"ابهج"],"; (S, A, K;) the latter of which is the more approved; (TA;) ",[1,"It"]," (a thing, TA, or an affair or event, S, A) ",[1,"rejoiced;"]," or ",[1,"made joyful, glad,"]," or ",[1,"happy;"]," (S, A, K;) a person. (S, A.)"],"f":"1"},{"h":"بهّج","t":["(ISd, L,) inf. n. ",[2,"تَبْهِيجٌ"],", (K,) ",[1