dliness:"]," (S, A, L, Msb, K:) or ",[1,"beauty of colour"]," of a thing: or its ",[1,"beauty and brightness"]," or ",[1,"splendour:"]," or in plants or herbage, ",[1,"beauty and brightness"]," or ",[1,"splendour;"]," and in a man, the ",[1,"laughing,"]," or ",[1,"happy, appearance of the beautiful parts of the face, as the cheeks, and the lines of the forehead:"]," or the ",[1,"appearance of joy, gladness,"]," or ",[1,"happiness;"]," or ",[1,"joyfulness, gladness,"]," or ",[1,"happiness, of aspect"]," or ",[1,"appearance."]," (L.) You say ",[2,"رَوْضَةٌ ذَاتُ بَهْجَةٍ غَالِبَةٍ"]," [",[1,"A meadow,"]," or ",[1,"garden, of surpassing beauty,"]," &c.]. (A.) And ",[2,"رَجُلٌ ذُو"],[2,"بَهْجَةٍ"],[1,"A man possessed of beauty,"]," or ",[1,"goodliness:"]," (S:) or ",[1,"of beauty and brightness,"]," &c. (L.) ― -b2- Also ",[1,"Happiness, joy,"]," or ",[1,"gladness."]," (Ham p. 403.)"]},{"h":"بَهِيجٌ","t":[[1,"Beautiful,"]," or ",[1,"goodly;"]," (S, A, L, Msb, K;) as also ↓ ",[2,"بَهِجٌ"]," (Ham p. 403) and ↓ ",[2,"بَهْجٌ"],": (AZ, TA:) or ",[1,"beautiful in colour:"]," or ",[1,"beautiful and bright"]," or ",[1,"splendid:"]," or, applied to a plant, it has this last meaning; and, applied to a man, ",[1,"characterized by a laughing,"]," or ",[1,"happy, appearance of the beautiful parts of the face, as the cheeks, and the lines of the forehead:"]," or ",[1,"characterized by the appearance of joy, gladness,"]," or ",[1,"happiness; having a joyful, glad,"]," or ",[1,"happy, aspect"]," or ",[1,"appearance:"]," (L:) the fem. epithet is ↓ ",[2,"مِبْهَاجٌ"],". (A, K, TA: [in the CK ",[2,"مَبْهاجٌ"],".]) It is applied to a plant, or herbage, (S, A,) in the Kur xxii. 5 and l. 7. (S.) And ↓ ",[2,"مِبْهَاجٌ"]," is applied to a woman, as meaning One ",[1,"in whom beauty,"]," or ",[1,"goodliness,"]," &c., ",[1,"predominates;"]," (L, TA;) as also ↓ ",[2,"بَهْجَةٌ"],"; (TA;) pl. of the former, ",[2,"مَبَاهِيجُ"],": (A, TA:) and to a camel's hump, meaning (tropical:) ",[1,"fat;"]," (A, K;) because beauty, or goodliness, is combined [in this case] with fatness; pl. as above. (A, TA.) ― -b2- See also ",[2,"بَهِجٌ"],"."]},{"h":"مِبْهَاجٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"بَهِيجٌ"],", in two places."]},{"h":"مُبْتَهِجٌ","t":[": see ",[2,"بَهِجٌ"],"."]}]},"maqayis":["الباء والهاء والجيم أصل واحد، وهو السرور والنضرة، يقال نبات بهيج، أي ناضر حسن. قال الله تعالى: {وأنبتنا فيها من كل زوج بهيج} [ق: 7] . والابتهاج السرور من ذلك أيضا."],"mufradat":["البهجة: حسن اللون وظهور السرور، وفيه قال عز وجل: حدائق ذات بهجة [النمل/ 60] ، وقد بهج فهو بهيج، قال: وأنبتنا فيها من كل زوج بهيج [ق/ 7] ، ويقال: بهج، كقول الشاعر: 69- ذات خلق بهج ولا يجيء منه بهوج، وقد ابتهج بكذا، أي: سر به سرورا بان أثره على وجهه، وأبهجه كذا."]}